From ff0971b74c30aeac0ca40f9729f14e5cca31b5e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emdee52 <emdee7101@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:10:53 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] port(SU-8): restrict the object-on-interface treatment to
 the contact a layer really rests on

The nominal contact polygons cover a whole organic overhang while the branch under it may touch a small patch, and _extrude treated a path as being in the footprint when any of its points was inside - one small contact slowed the whole perimeter loop and the whole layer (41581 object moves at 50 percent, outer wall 28095). Record the printed contact per layer in the toolpath stage and run the joint-2 pass after it (object lslices intersect that footprint), and treat a path only when at least half of its points are inside. Slowed moves drop to 2093 (outer wall 150, slowed layers 135 -> 1); the per-layer temperature delta is unchanged.
---
 src/libslic3r/GCode.cpp                 | 12 ++--
 src/libslic3r/Support/SupportCommon.cpp | 88 ++++++++++++++-----------
 2 files changed, 57 insertions(+), 43 deletions(-)

